Talos kernel patch for Radxa TACO boards (talos-builds, kernels/rpi_cm-radxa_taco/patches).

Raspberry Pi's MSI-X support for the BCM2711/BCM2712 PCIe controller's internal MSI
target, as carried in raspberrypi/linux since 2025-04-02 (commit 831b46008fa4, in
rpi-6.18.y). Mainline's pcie-brcmstb offers only MSI and multi-MSI, so every device falls
back from MSI-X to MSI. The NVMe on the CM4 TACO (SK hynix Gold P31) does not work on MSI:
its admin commands complete but no interrupt arrives ("QID 0 timeout, completion polled")
and the boot stalls; with MSI-X under Raspberry Pi OS it works. Evidence:
kernels/rpi_cm-radxa_taco/README.md (Raspberry Pi OS 6.18.50+rpt on the same board, directly and through
Talos's U-Boot). With this, `pci=nomsi` can go from the CM4's kernel arguments.

Applied by siderolabs/pkgs' kernel-build step (kernel/build/pkg.yaml applies every
kernel/build/patches/*.patch with patch -p1). Drop it once Talos's kernel carries a fix.

From: Jonathan Bell <jonathan@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Apr 2025 15:25:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: pcie-brcmstb: fake MSIx support on internal MSI target

Apparently some NVMe SSD implementations don't fall back to MSI cleanly,
instead making the driver allocate one queue via the legacy interrupt.

There are still only 32 vectors available, but should be sufficient for
the majority of use-cases on BCM2711.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Bell <jonathan@raspberrypi.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c
@@ -473,7 +473,8 @@ static void brcm_pcie_set_outbound_win(struct brcm_pcie *pcie,
 				 MSI_FLAG_NO_AFFINITY)

 #define BRCM_MSI_FLAGS_SUPPORTED (MSI_GENERIC_FLAGS_MASK	| \
-				  MSI_FLAG_MULTI_PCI_MSI)
+				  MSI_FLAG_MULTI_PCI_MSI	| \
+				  MSI_FLAG_PCI_MSIX)

 static const struct msi_parent_ops brcm_msi_parent_ops = {
 	.required_flags		= BRCM_MSI_FLAGS_REQUIRED,
